Security Critical: yes

With min and max replaced respectively with __min and __max. See below for an explanation.

---

These headers are almost the equivalent of WTL 8.0 from http://sourceforge.net/projects/wtl/
with patch #1871358 applied.
http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?func=detail&aid=1871358&group_id=109071&atid=652374

"Fixes support for building with NOMINMAX defined.
When defining NOMINMAX before including windows.h, min and max aren't
defined. __min and __max are always defined though. So use them instead.

This patch simply consist of a search of replace for both term."

---

Cherry pick of http://sourceforge.net/tracker/index.php?func=detail&aid=1871358&group_id=109071&atid=652374

---

Local: warnings MSVC has started emitting since WTL 8.0 was published, fixed
here rather than suppressed, because suppressing them would also hide the same
mistakes in Sawbuck's own code. All are spelling fixes with no behaviour
change; WTL 10 carries equivalent ones upstream.

  atlmisc.h, atldlgs.h -- C4302, 'type cast': truncation from LPCTSTR to WORD.
    _U_STRINGorID::m_lpstr holds either a string or an INTRESOURCE, i.e. a
    small integer in a pointer, and these sites want the integer. Casting a
    pointer straight to WORD is ill-formed on Win64; (WORD)(ULONG_PTR) is the
    cast the Windows SDK itself uses. Every site is already guarded by
    IS_INTRESOURCE or by an ATLASSERT on the ID range.

  atlgdi.h -- C4706, assignment used as a condition. AtlGetDibBitmap tests
    the result of CreateDIBSection inline; parenthesised and compared against
    NULL, which is what the warning asks for.
